# Loaded only by `npm run build:netlify` (Vite's `--mode netlify`), where it
# beats `.env` - so the localhost default below it can never win by accident.
#
# RELATIVE on purpose. Vite bakes this string into the bundle, so an absolute
# URL would tie one build to one customer's API host. A relative base makes
# every request go to whichever host served the page; Netlify's `/api/*` proxy
# in netlify.toml forwards it to the real API. That also keeps the browser
# seeing ONE origin, which is what lets the session and CSRF cookies stay
# SameSite=Lax instead of needing SameSite=None.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api/v1
